---
import PageLayout from "blume/components/layout/PageLayout.astro";
import data from "blume:data";
const { config } = data;
---
<PageLayout site={{ title: config.title, description: config.description }} logo={{ ...data.logo, dimensions: { light: { width: 1280, height: 1280 }, dark: { width: 1280, height: 1280 } } }} navigation={data.navigation} favicon={data.favicon} fontCssVars={data.fontCssVars} themeMode={config.theme.mode} searchEnabled={config.search.enabled} siteUrl={config.site} ogEnabled={config.og.enabled} page={{ title: "openlaunch — Connect your agents to your hardware", description: config.description }}>
<main class="workbench">
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>Connect your agents<br />to your hardware.</h1>
    <p>openlaunch is an open source bridge for ChatGPT, Codex, and other agents. Run it on your machine, pair a board, and choose what the agent can do. Start with a health check, an LED, or a message on your Uno's matrix.</p>
    <p class="note">Developer alpha. Local MCP works today. Hosted ChatGPT setup and real board testing are still in progress.</p>
    <nav class="links"><a href="/docs/setup">Get started →</a><a href="https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch">GitHub ↗</a><a href="/docs/resources">Downloads & resources →</a></nav>
  </section>
  <section class="boards" aria-label="Hardware setup">
    <article><a href="/docs/uno-r4"><img src="/images/uno-r4-wifi.webp" alt="Generated monochrome illustration of an Uno R4 WiFi board" width="1536" height="1024" /></a><h2>Uno R4 WiFi</h2><p>Check health, toggle the built-in LED, and write ASCII text to the matrix. Stock and repaired console-mux profiles have separate builds.</p><div class="links"><a href="/docs/uno-r4">Set up your Uno →</a><a href="https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch/tree/main/firmware">Firmware ↗</a></div></article>
    <article><a href="/docs/pi"><img src="/images/raspberry-pi-4.webp" alt="Generated monochrome illustration of a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B" width="1536" height="1024" /></a><h2>Raspberry Pi 4</h2><p>Run the Go agent on a 4GB or 8GB Model B. The real runtime reports health. GPIO and display support are future work.</p><div class="links"><a href="/docs/pi">Set up your Pi →</a><a href="https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch/tree/main/devices/pi">Go agent ↗</a></div></article>
  </section>
  <p class="image-note">Generated hardware illustrations. Use the manufacturer pinouts for wiring.</p>
  <section class="start"><div><h2>Try it locally</h2><p>Node 24+ and Go are required. This builds the owner console and runs a simulated device test without a board.</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch.git
cd openlaunch
npm ci
npm run build --workspace @openlaunch/web
npm run test:e2e</code></pre><a href="/docs/setup">Start the bridge and connect Codex →</a></div><div><h2>Then pair a board</h2><p>Start the local bridge, open the console, and create an enrollment. Use the board's setup guide to pair it, then grant your agent a capability and request health.</p><p>Enrollment expires in 10 minutes and can be used once. Pairing doesn't grant agent access. Commands poll every 10 seconds; inspect the completed result.</p><div class="links"><a href="/docs/uno-r4">Uno guide →</a><a href="/docs/pi">Pi guide →</a><a href="/docs/pairing">Permission details →</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="build"><h2>Hack on it</h2><p>Protocol, auth, HTTP, MCP, and hardware adapters are independent packages. Add a capability or another device without tying firmware to an AI provider.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch/tree/main/packages">Shared packages ↗</a><a href="/docs/architecture">Architecture →</a><a href="/docs/resources">SDKs, OS images & tools →</a><a href="/docs/status">What's working →</a></div><p class="note">The public site serves docs. Device controls stay local until hosted authentication is complete.</p></section>
</main>
</PageLayout>
<style is:global>
.workbench{max-width:1040px;margin:auto;padding:48px 36px 70px;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace;color:#111;background:#fff}.workbench *{box-sizing:border-box}.workbench h1{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,48px);line-height:1.18;letter-spacing:-2px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 22px}.workbench h2{font-size:26px;letter-spacing:-1px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 16px}.workbench p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 20px}.intro>p{max-width:780px}.workbench .note,.image-note{font-size:11px;color:#666}.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px 24px}.workbench a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px;font-size:13px}.workbench a:hover{opacity:.65}.workbench a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid currentColor;outline-offset:5px}.boards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:36px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;margin-top:36px;padding-top:24px}.boards img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin-bottom:24px;filter:grayscale(1)}.boards p{font-size:13px}.image-note{margin:20px 0!important}.start{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-top:1px solid #ccc;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;margin-top:30px}.start>div{padding:32px 0}.start>div+div{border-left:1px solid #ccc;padding-left:30px;margin-left:30px}.start p,.build p{font-size:13px}.workbench pre{background:#f3f3f3;border:1px solid #ddd;padding:18px;overflow:auto;font-size:11px;line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:22px}.build{padding-top:32px}.build>p{max-width:760px}.build .note{margin-top:28px}:root[data-theme='dark'] .workbench,:root.dark .workbench{color:#eee;background:#111}.dark .workbench pre,[data-theme='dark'] .workbench pre{background:#1a1a1a;border-color:#444}.dark .workbench .note,[data-theme='dark'] .workbench .note{color:#aaa}.dark .boards img,[data-theme='dark'] .boards img{mix-blend-mode:screen}.dark .workbench [class], [data-theme='dark'] .workbench [class]{border-color:#444}@media(max-width:650px){.workbench{padding:30px 20px}.workbench h1{letter-spacing:-1px}.boards,.start{grid-template-columns:1fr}.boards{gap:34px}.start>div+div{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid #ccc;padding-left:0;margin-left:0}.links{gap:14px 20px}}
</style>
<style is:global>
html{filter:grayscale(1)}
.dark img[src='/icon.png'],[data-theme='dark'] img[src='/icon.png']{filter:grayscale(1) invert(1)}
</style>
